<resources>
    <!--
      Dark parent, not DayNight. This style only ever paints the pre-Compose LAUNCH WINDOW —
      the frame the OS shows before the first composition runs and VeldtTheme (see Theme.kt)
      resolves the user's actual Light/Dark/Follow-system choice from DataStore. That choice
      is not synchronously readable here, so this style cannot reflect it and is pinned dark.

      KNOWN LIMITATION: a user who has explicitly chosen Light theme sees a dark launch frame
      for one frame on cold start, before Compose applies their choice and repaints. This is
      not correct, only chosen over the alternative — a DayNight parent would instead show a
      WHITE launch frame to every Dark-theme and Follow-system-in-dark user, which is worse for
      more people on the common path. A real fix needs a synchronously-readable cached theme
      preference plus `setTheme()` before `super.onCreate()` in MainActivity; out of scope for
      this pass pending a measurement of how visible the flash actually is on a device.

      statusBarColor stays transparent for the same window: MainActivity's enableEdgeToEdge()
      sets the runtime value, but the theme is what the launch frame is drawn with.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.Veldt" parent="Theme.Material3.DynamicColors.Dark">
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
    </style>
</resources>
